  "summary": "Both previous proposals correctly identify the core problem but each has gaps. The first proposal suggests storing human feedback as impl_review entries, which the second rightly warns could be overwritten by subsequent automated reviews. The second proposes a dedicated human_feedback field but doesn't address the critical TUI bug where full_feedback is constructed on line 3008 but never persisted. The simplest correct fix involves three targeted changes: (1) Add a 'human_rejection_feedback' field to FeatureFile (state.py) with set/get methods - this is stored separately from impl_reviews so it can't be overwritten by automated reviews. (2) In tui.py line 3008-3011, after building full_feedback, call feature.set_human_rejection_feedback(full_feedback) before save() - this fixes the TUI path where feedback is built but discarded. (3) In phases.py's _get_latest_feedback() function (line 609), check human_rejection_feedback FIRST before checking impl_reviews - if it exists, return it and clear it after consumption so it doesn't persist through subsequent review cycles. For the web UI path: (a) the moveFeatureData struct in api.go needs a 'reason' field, (b) the web UI needs a simple text prompt modal on reject (similar to TUI's RejectModal), (c) the server-to-TUI websocket message must forward the reason, and (d) the TUI's server message handler (line 2168) must store the reason via the same human_rejection_feedback field and route to 'implementing' not 'rejected'. This approach requires ~6 small edits across 4 files, avoids any schema changes to the existing review arrays, and ensures both TUI and web UI rejections flow through the same feedback path that agents already consume."
